// Two modules each define a type `Bag` with a method `put` of different shape: in `shapes2d` it takes
// an `f32` and mutates the receiver (implicit `self`), in `shapes3d` it takes no argument. Each call must use its own
// type's signature (type identity is module-qualified, never the bare type name). Expected by hand:
// two puts in each module.
// expect: 2 2
mod shapes2d
mod shapes3d

fn main() {
    let a = shapes2d::bag::filled()
    let b = shapes3d::bag::filled()
    println("${a.count} ${b.count}")
}
